     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : past simple ou present perfect",
     "statement": "Choisis : Amina (visit) her aunt last Sunday.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "« last Sunday » est un moment précis et terminé."
      },
      {
       "md": "On emploie le past simple."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Amina visited her aunt last Sunday.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : past perfect",
     "statement": "Relie : Boris went home. He finished his homework before. (when)",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Finir les devoirs vient en premier : past perfect."
      },
      {
       "md": "Aller à la maison : past simple."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**When Boris went home, he had finished his homework.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Erreurs fréquentes",
     "md": "- « I have seen him yesterday » → I **saw** him yesterday.\n- « I had went » → I had **gone**.\n- Utiliser le past perfect quand il n'y a qu'une seule action passée : « I had eaten rice » seul, sans repère, est rarement nécessaire.\n- Confondre since (point de départ) et for (durée)."
    }
