     "title": "Propositions de temps",
     "md": "Après **when, as soon as, before, after, until, if**, on emploie le **présent simple** (pas will) pour parler du futur.\n- I will call you **as soon as I arrive**.\n- **When** she **finishes**, we will go out."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : proposition de temps",
     "statement": "Complète : I will phone you when I (arrive).",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Après when : présent simple."
      },
      {
       "md": "Sujet I : arrive."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**I will phone you when I arrive.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : choix de forme",
     "statement": "Look at the sky ! It (rain). Quelle forme ?",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Il y a un signe visible : be going to."
      },
      {
       "md": "On relit la phrase obtenue pour vérifier la forme du verbe et le sens."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**It is going to rain.**"
    },
